# The change classes that wait for the maintainer even into `staging`
# (AGENTS.md, "Four kinds of change still wait for the maintainer"). The
# `staging` ruleset requires a code owner's review, so a PR touching any path
# below cannot merge on green checks alone — for any identity without the
# admin role. An interactive agent session acts as the maintainer's own account, so
# for it this is discipline, not a rule (AGENTS.md). A path not listed here has
# no owner and merges on the ruleset's other rules.
#
# Later lines win, and no line here shadows another: each names one class.

# The permission surface: workflows and the composites that run inside them.
/.github/workflows/ @modelmirror
/.github/actions/ @modelmirror

# The security posture, its setup, and the authorization check that enforces
# it (`authorize-trigger` and the tests that pin the trigger surface).
